# Build interfaces and documentation with Roc

Roc plus Datastar host a web application. `.rocci` templates are HTML for Roc.
Applications add a server. Rocdown is an optional document layer — more
experimental than templates.

:card-grid.begin
    :link-card[page: "docs/start/five-minutes", title: "Preview a template", summary: "Lower and view a checked-in @component. No server required."]
    :link-card[page: "docs/tutorials/first-app", title: "Run an application", summary: "Standalone .rocci server, or custom main.roc that reuses modules."]
    :link-card[page: "rocdown/index", title: "Author a document", summary: "Markdown-first pages. Experimental; live pages reuse Applications."]
    :link-card[page: "examples/index", title: "Examples", summary: "Inspect complete Rocci apps and their published source."]
    :link-card[page: "project/status", title: "Project status", summary: "See what works now, the deliberate limits, and the adoption boundary."]
:card-grid.end

## See the model in one minute

Author a `.rocci` view as a pure Roc function, serve semantic HTML, and add Datastar actions only where an interaction needs them. For prose-led work, keep articles in `.rocdown` and presentation in a project theme.

- [The stack](/docs/the-stack/)
- [Preview a component](/docs/start/five-minutes/)
- [Author a Rocdown page](/rocdown/pages/)
- [Study complete examples](/examples/)

## Try the shipped hybrid path

The card below is the [live counter](/examples/live-counter/) app composed into this page: CDN snapshot HTML, then `GET /sse` keeps the shared count and recent click origins in sync across tabs. Place comes from your browser timezone or a chosen override — neither is verified.

@render LiveCounterUi.CounterIsland({ count: 0.I64, clicks: LiveCounterUi.empty_clicks, show_reset: False })
<div data-init=@get("/sse", [OpenWhenHidden(True)])></div>

## Know the maturity boundary

Rocci is an active experiment. The compiler, local runtime, Rocdown site generator, hybrid serving path, editor integration, and local macOS bundling work today. Production distribution and broad cross-platform validation are not complete. Read [Project status](/project/status/) before adopting it.
